<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hallein</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hallein is a town on the Salzach in the Austrian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>, south of the city of Salzburg. Its salt mine on the Dürrnberg, already worked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, was the main source of the prince-archbishops' wealth. Mining continued until 1989, and the Celtic finds are shown in the town's museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hallein.jpg" alt="Hallein" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hallein_vom_Barmstoa2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
